# nr-relay-native-push: what the wiring applies (nothing here was compiled: cargo was not run)

No hot file is edited by this task: Cargo.toml of mixdog-relay already carries every crate it uses (p256 with ecdsa, pkcs8 and
pem; ring; pem; reqwest with http2; base64; url; serde_json; mixdog-fsio; mixdog-js; and tempfile as a dev-dependency), so there
is no Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock or workspace-hack edit and no protocol row. SERVICE_PENDING in compose_flip.rs: no name leaves it.

## What the tasks that assemble the relay use (mixdog_relay::native_push)

- `NativePush::from_environment(&config.env)` builds the credentialed sender for the process (real hosts, system clock,
  reqwest transport) and logs "[relay] APNs credentials unusable: <msg>" or "[relay] FCM credentials unusable: <msg>" for a
  platform it disables. nr-relay-server wraps it as `Option<Arc<dyn PushSender>>`, `None` when `is_configured()` is false
  (Node passed `null`), and builds one `NativePushService::new(that)` shared by every desktop leg.
- `NativePushService` replaces `nativePush` + `nativeBindings` + `nativeLimiter` of the leg context (120 sends a minute per
  device is built in; `with_limiter` takes another RateLimiter):
  - `platforms()`: the `nativePushPlatforms` for `relay-capabilities` (`nativePush: 1` and `nativePushPlatforms` are sent only
    when it is not empty).
  - `bind(device_id, &dyn PairedClients, &frame)` for `native-push-bind`, `unbind(device_id, &frame)` for
    `native-push-unbind`, `drop_bindings(device_id, Some(client_id) | None)` for `dropNativeBindings` on `revoke-client` and
    on a revoked device, `send(device_id, &dyn PairedClients, &frame).await -> Option<Value>` for `native-push`: the leg writes
    the returned `native-push-result` frame with js::wire; `None` (no credentials) writes nothing.
  - `PairedClients` is implemented by the legs over the device store: `has_client(device_id, client_id)` is
    `store.hasClient(...) === true`.
  - `close()` at relay shutdown (Node's `nativePush.close()`).
- The twin host fakes the sender at the trait seam: implement `PushSender` (platforms, send, close) as tests/native_push.rs's
  FakePush does, or hand `NativePush::new` a recording `HttpTransport` with `Origins`.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/Cargo.toml (scaffold file, not edited here)

tests/native_push.rs calls two items that exist only with the `test-support` feature (`NativePushService::hold_single_association`
and `association_count`), so a bare `cargo test` would not compile it. Add beside the `twin` entry:

    [[test]]
    name = "native_push"
    path = "tests/native_push.rs"
    required-features = ["test-support"]
